WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.090
Welcome to the Microsoft for Education Daily, Saturday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.510
Let's catch you up on everything new from Microsoft.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.950
Use what you have. In Wales,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.910
the schools platform Hwb just got a fresh, simpler look.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.210
Plus, learners and teachers still get Microsoft 365 free on their own devices.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.680
In class, Teams will let you open a busy channel at your last read message,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.580
due February.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.320
Odd guest invite?

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.010
You can now report it to IT straight from Teams, as it rolls out.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.250
Coding class?

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.860
GitHub Desktop now signs in to more than one account on the same site.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:58.900
Keep personal and uni accounts side by side; each repo knows which to use.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.490
For university AI labs, a coming Windows preview links PCs with USB4 cables.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.590
In Microsoft's lab, three mini PCs ran a 235-billion-parameter model together.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.890
Prefer the cloud? Foundry's Managed Compute,

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.830
for open models, is now generally available.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.750
And web developers can now try Edge's built-in AI model, Aion, on a live site.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.830
For school IT,

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:35.910
Teams will let you pick which outside notetaker bots join your meetings, due January.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.050
And Edge will install waiting updates when the browser's idle, also due January.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.630
The fine print? From mid-December,

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.580
new Teams releases need iOS or iPadOS 18 or later.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.630
And personal Windows 11 PCs are now getting 26H2 automatically, bit by bit.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.260
After hours, build tiny factories on floating islands in Jaden Industries,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.500
out November 23.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.900
Then Cat Mirror has you steer two cats at once, and every move is mirrored.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.390
Plus Sokobear Goo, with 40 puzzle levels, and Gravity SWITCH, with 50 stages.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.480
A home laptop, spare PCs, the accounts you've got: use what you have.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.820
Every day, the changelog gets a little longer.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.800
Check the board: shipped today, and more on the way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.690
All of that, in one day. And it keeps on shipping.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.950
That's the Microsoft for Education Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.
